+# Circleback Task 4 source and verification report
+
+## Official sources inspected 28 October 2026
+- https://circleback.ai/docs/api : base https://circleback.ai/api; bearer supplied API key. RFC8288 Link rel=next, opaque cursor. Account-wide limits, 429 Retry-After seconds. No key created or used.
+- https://circleback.ai/docs/api/meetings/list-meetings : GET /meetings; query ownership All/Mine/Shared (default Mine), statuses[], cursor, tagIds[], attendeeProfileIds[]. Response bare meeting array, NOT a data wrapper.
+- https://circleback.ai/docs/api/meetings/get-meeting : GET /meeting/{meetingId}; response bare meeting object. Read permission determines included details.
+- https://circleback.ai/docs/api/meetings/get-meeting-transcript : GET /meeting/{meetingId}/transcript; bare array of {speaker:string,text:string,timestamp:number}, timestamps fractional seconds (example4.56).
+
+List/detail examples: id/name strings; createdAt/updatedAt ISO dates; duration number; url/recordingUrl/icalUid strings; tags[{id,name,description}]; attendees[{profileId,name,title,companyName,email,isCalendarEventOrganizer,isCalendarInvitee}]; notes/privateNotes strings; actionItems[{id,title,description,assignee nullable person,status}]. The client projects these fields only. Insights (heterogeneous JSON), linkAccess, calendarEvent and sharedWith appear in docs but are deliberately not projected for Task4. Unknown fields ignored. RecordingUrl is inert data, never fetched. No standalone notes/action mutation or search/list-action API implemented.
+
+The docs rendered browser examples use circleback.ai/api; text extraction misleadingly showed example.com in generated snippets, so actual browser endpoint labels were checked. API base GET404 is not missing documentation.
+
+## Public signatures
+Namespace OpenClicky.Providers.Circleback.
+- CirclebackClient(Func<CancellationToken, ValueTask<string?>> tokenAccessor, HttpMessageHandler? handler = null, int maxResponseBytes = 4194304)
+- Task<CirclebackMeetingPage> ListMeetingsAsync(Uri? nextPage = null, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)
+- Task<CirclebackMeetingResult> GetMeetingAsync(string meetingId, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)
+- Task<CirclebackTranscriptResult> GetTranscriptAsync(string meetingId, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)
+- void Dispose()
+
+DTO signatures are positional records in CirclebackModels.cs. Source is CirclebackSource(Uri Endpoint, DateTimeOffset RetrievedAt). Meeting detail returns Meeting+Source, list Meetings+NextPage+Source, transcript MeetingId+Segments+Source. Errors: CirclebackException.Kind/StatusCode/RetryAfter; kinds Revoked,RateLimited,Unavailable,UnsafeEndpoint,MalformedResponse,ResponseTooLarge,RequestFailed.
+
+Transport uses dedicated no-cookie, no-redirect SocketsHttpHandler by default; known auto-redirect HttpClientHandler/SocketsHttpHandler rejected. Arbitrary injected custom handlers are trusted transport infrastructure, not a security boundary: they must not independently forward requests. No caller HttpClient or mutable base URL. Response timeout60 seconds, header32KiB default transport, body4MiB configurable1..16MiB; count10000; JSON depth32; page links8192; IDs1..256 ASCII safe characters. No automatic retry or full-account pagination. Caller token accessor must return a protected credential just in time; credential not persisted/logged. Response bodies and underlying transport exceptions are not copied into errors.
+
+## Verification
+Initial fixture-first build: exit1, expected missing Circleback namespace/types; this was compile-red, not runtime-red.
+Initial implemented focused suite: exit0,26/26.
+Additional malformed transcript regression: exit1,33 pass1 fail; missing timestamp incorrectly defaulted0. Fixed using JsonRequired.
+Further focused/full results recorded below.
+
+## Acceptance boundary
+Real account access, entitlement, API key validity, actual provider payloads and caller integration are UNVERIFIED. Tests use injected HttpMessageHandler with synthetic tokens only. No real API calls, key creation, media downloads, writes, UI, integration or global configuration changes.
+
